    <Folder>
      <name>Intelligence Summary</name>
      <Placemark>
        <name>AI Council Assessment</name>
        <styleUrl>#intel</styleUrl>
        <description>The synthesized intelligence assessment reveals a U.S. military posture characterized by high operational tempo, strategic repositioning, and significant resource strain. Carrier strike groups and amphibious ready groups are concentrated in the Western Pacific and Eastern Pacific, with forward-deployed assets in Japan and the Philippines, reflecting a focus on countering Chinese maritime assertiveness in the South China Sea. The USS Nimitz is undergoing decommissioning, while newer carriers like the Gerald R. Ford and John F. Kennedy are either deployed or in final construction phases, indicating a transition in carrier fleet composition. The depletion of long-range missile stockpiles—including THAAD, ATACMS, and Patriot interceptors—following the Iran conflict underscores severe resource constraints and potential vulnerabilities in U.S. strategic deterrence capabilities. Maritime patrol and ISR operations in the Gulf of Mexico and Caribbean indicate sustained counter-narcotics and regional security efforts, while European operations show a mix of ISR and logistics flights supporting NATO commitments. The establishment of a permanent U.S. military base in Poland further highlights NATO’s Eastern flank reinforcement amid rising tensions with Russia. Overall, the data suggests a U.S. military actively engaged in multiple theaters, balancing forward presence with modernization efforts while navigating significant inventory depletion and strategic realignment.</description>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>0,0,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
    </Folder>
